A||||7||1FieroGTRacingInc||glasspack's = ricer???||||5||
Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||11-16-2000||06:24 PM||||does anyone have a set of glasspack's on there v-6??  how does it sound??  like a ricemobile???  i hope not, i was thinking about running true dual's using the glasspack's...  ohh  I also picked me up a garrett t-3  turbo from a turbo t-bird that had 34,700 miles on it($100) So I'll be doing some custom exhaust work anyway...<BR>OR...... <BR>Running a set of true dual's using two flowmaster 40 series...  Which would be beter using that turbo also....  I had already picked up a smaller turbo from the 2.0l sunbrd turbo...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> What about having a 3.4L w/true dual's and...   TWIN TURBO'S????   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">     Is it POSSIBLE??     steve he he he||||reg||5
Z||000001||msweldon||11-17-2000||03:24 PM||||I have a true dual exhaust w/ glasspacks on my "basicly" stock 2.8.  Lost tq, but it sounded awesome with the V6 until the fiberglass was burned and blownout.  If you do decide to go with glasspacks go with one that will last somewhat longer than the ones from off the shelf at pep-boys, like mine. Go with Dynomax Turbo series or equivalent.  If you do go with duals, research the possible need for a H-pipe.  Mine has all sorts of scavaging issues.  Letting off the throttle after a good rev will make all sorts of popping noises as if it is back-firing.<P>I'll recommend all other information be requested from 1FST2M6, he's working on a 3.4 Bi-turbo setup.  He's also rather astute about exhaust systems and could answer most of your questions.<P>marc<BR><p>[This message has been edited by msweldon (edited 11-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-17-2000||04:27 PM||||thanks Marc!<P>you can use "true dual exhaust" but your turbos will have to be the same size. if your gunna use one from a 2.0 probly a T-25 or 28 with a weak a/r. and a T3 you'll have to plum them in series like the Quad turbo Ferrari Testarossa(sp) that Koenig built in the late 80s run #1 and #2 in to turbo #1 and run cyl 3456 in to the T3. it's really way more work than any performance gain you'll see or feel. just one T-3 will support 250ish but you'll have a REALLY high charge air temp cause the turbo will be working it's little head off to keep up with the 32+lbs of air your 2.8 needs. your best bet would be the single T3 you have, using ported manifolds, sprint manifolds or chris west shorty headers, into the turbo with at LEAST 3" down pipe fron the turbo in to a 3" cat (if required in your area) and on to a 3" muffler.  Like Marc said the packing WON'T last long. unless you have a Brullen, Dynomax or Powertone, they use stainless mesh to hold the 'glas or carbon packing in. you might want to check out <A HREF="http://www.spintechmufflers.com" TARGET=_blank>www.spintechmufflers.com</A>  also. they are quiet and flow well and don't resonate in the car like a cherry bomb! You got a good deal on that turbo! Nice find!  i'd shy away from the duals though. nothing wrong with them.. just not that great fo our tiny engines.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||11-18-2000||03:35 PM||||FieroGTRacing...<P>If your name is accurate, it doesnt matter if it sounds ricey!<P>Heck I would make my car ricey it helped...<BR>If I could shave off 3/10  of a second off my lap times by putting a coffee can on the back I would.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||11-19-2000||12:05 AM||||I had considered true dual exhaust until I heard one. It was on a 3.8 on top of that so I thought it would sound truely awesome. <P>When I heard it I went Awe but not necessarily in a good way. The uneven exhaust pulses made a popping noise similar to a cylinder missing. I knew he wasn't missing a cylinder so it was a let down. Car ran like a bat out of hell but at idle it just made a "put-put" sound. <P>If you can, try to connect the pipes somehow...in certain publications for hot rodding there is a show of improvement taking a dual exhuast and having a crossover. <P>When I did my exhuast on a built up 2.8 (done before I knew about 3.4 grr!) I went with the 2.5 inch mandral bent exhuast without mufflers, but keeping the cat. Unfortuanately for me right now the cat got blown out and the resonator tips are barely keeping me from being lynched by the neighbors! Plus the resonance inside the car is enough make your ears ring going up hill.<P>Im going to go with a good sized glasspack instead of cat flanged for smog purposes and see if it takes the low frequencies out of the driver's compartment. <P>Hope this helps you out with your question!<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000005||Raydar||11-19-2000||12:26 AM||||My Formula has a cat, single glasspack, and dual resonators. It resonates enough to set off car alarms in the parking deck, at work. (Security must <I>love</I> me.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> If it was any louder inside the car, I would consider it unpleasant. <BR>Next time, I'll probably do a single Flowmaster. <BR>Just my $.02. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>"You want me to do <I>what</I>!? <BR>If I could do <I>that</I> I'd never leave the house!"||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||11-19-2000||12:34 AM||||THANK'S FOR THE INFO GUY'S...<BR>I DID  find a second T-3 Garrett with 100,000 miles on it, so it will be rebuilt first.  <BR>1FST2M6....    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> he he...  are you working on using the T-3 Garrett's for your TWIN  turbo conversion??  would you plumb 1 turbo from each ex. manifold??  steve||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||11-19-2000||12:41 AM||||I have a true dual exhaust with "turbo tube" glass pack mufflers. They look like a straight through glass pack, but are a lot bigger around and have the turbo muffler like pipes inside. The car has a very aggressive sound to it, sort of like the stock system only louder at higher speeds. <BR>Because of the even, bank to bank firing of the 60 degree engine, the duals do not resonate like they would on a different engine.||||reg||1
